      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The involvement of bacterial lipopolysaccharides in the induction of atherogenesis is postulated. The excess of bacterial lipopolysaccharides (endotoxin aggression) is observed in the general blood circulation of volunteers with the presence of atherosclerotic risk factors (obesity, diabetes, stress, pathology of haemostasis, kidney, intestines, etc.). The results allow to be optimistic about the prospects for preventing the development and progression of atherosclerotic pathology."},
